Fluid Mechanics — David Tong (@fd-tong: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA
David Tong. Fluid Mechanics, University of Cambridge lecture notes. [Current author page and complete notes](https://davidtong.org/teaching/fluid-mechanics/) · [Historical author rights notice](https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/fluids/).

Study the complete notes, following derivations and solving unfamiliar variants. The website presents five download parts, but the inspected PDF contents number six chapters: 1 Introduction, 2 Inviscid Flows, 3 The Navier–Stokes Equation, 4 Waves, 5 Instabilities and 6 Turbulence. Assignments here follow that PDF numbering. The separately published expanded textbook is a different edition.

The historical author page permits attributed, unaltered, noncommercial distribution; this is not a CC adaptation licence. The full PDF exceeded the browser's size limit, but all five individual PDFs opened and the contents were checked. Preserve the actual version and credited material. Classical papers linked by the author are separate sources. No source copy is bundled.

